.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt TZFSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzfsd
.Nd "[TZFS] storage daemon"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl c Ar config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the
.Sy [TZFS]
system daemon that owns the storage plane of the capability system.
It holds the root-pool handle for the pool that backs
.Pa /Capabilities ,
auto-provisions the persistent, ephemeral, and template dataset roots, and
maintains a curated set of storage
.Em flavors .
On request it mints a rights-limited TrustedZFS handle
.Pq see Xr trustedzfs 3
and passes it back to the caller over
.Dv SCM_RIGHTS ;
the caller then drives the handle with the ordinary verb interface.
.Nm
takes the storage-granting role that
.Xr authorityd 8
previously performed inline.
.Pp
ZFS is a required subsystem for this system, although the host may still boot
from UFS.
.Nm
comes up in the PID 1 boot chain, after the pool is available and before
.Xr serviced 8
hands out storage to services.
.Pp
All name-based setup
.Pq configuration, opening the pool, provisioning, receiving baked templates
happens at startup.
.Nm
then enters capability mode with
.Xr cap_enter 2
and serves every request from its retained capability handles, so a
compromised daemon cannot reach datasets outside
.Pa /Capabilities .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fl c Ar config"
.It Fl c Ar config
Read configuration from
.Ar config
instead of
.Pa /etc/capability/tzfsd.ucl .
A missing file is not an error; built-in defaults stand.
.It Fl f
Run in the foreground and log to stderr as well as syslog.
.El
.Sh FLAVORS
A flavor is a template dataset cloned per request (instant, copy-on-write).
The out-of-the-box set is:
.Bl -tag -width ".Sy freebsd" -offset indent
.It Sy empty
a bare dataset, built live.
.It Sy native
a 5BSD base userland.
.It Sy freebsd
a FreeBSD base rootfs.
.It Sy linux
a Rocky Linux 9 rootfs, offered as a directory and enabled by default.
.El
.Pp
A flavor whose template cannot be made available
.Pq not baked, not built, or disabled in configuration
is simply not offered, and a request for it fails with
.Er ENOENT .
The
.Sy linux
flavor is on by default but may be removed to slim a deployment; see
.Xr tzfs.conf 5 .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /var/run/tzfsd.ready" -compact
.It Pa /etc/capability/tzfsd.ucl
configuration file
.It Pa /var/run/tzfsd.sock
request socket (root only)
.It Pa /var/run/tzfsd.ready
readiness marker, written once serving begins
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr libtzfsd 3 ,
.Xr trustedzfs 3 ,
.Xr tzfs.conf 5 ,
.Xr tzfsctl 8 ,
.Xr authorityd 8 ,
.Xr serviced 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
